response.value:
The real-time suggestion stops working after you remove the `<div class="mt-6">...</div>` because your JavaScript contains this line:

```javascript
document.getElementById('results-per-page').addEventListener('change', (e) => {
  resultsPerPage = e.target.value;
  // Do not auto-fetch terms, just update value
});
```

When you remove the `<select id="results-per-page" ...>`, this line tries to attach an event listener to an element that no longer exists. This causes a JavaScript error, which stops the rest of your script from running—including the real-time suggestion logic.

**How to fix:**  
Remove or comment out this line in your script:

```javascript
document.getElementById('results-per-page').addEventListener('change', (e) => {
  resultsPerPage = e.target.value;
  // Do not auto-fetch terms, just update value
});
```

This will prevent the error and allow the rest of your JavaScript (including real-time suggestions) to work correctly.

